msgid "Task Attributes"
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:167
msgid "Difficulty"
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:167
msgid "Perceived complexity level (1-5)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:168
msgid "Established Duration"
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:168
msgid "Days and hours estimated for completion."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:170
msgid "User Invitation"
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:171
msgid ""
"The system allows inviting people who do not yet have an account to "
"participate in a task:"
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:173
msgid ""
"During task creation or editing, the user can invite by entering the guest's "
"email."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:174
msgid ""
"The system sends an automatic email with task details and a unique "
"registration link. This link expires after 48 hours."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:175
msgid ""
"As soon as the guest completes registration through the received link, they "
"are automatically linked to the task with the pre-assigned role."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:177
msgid "Share via Link"
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:178
msgid ""
"In addition to email invitations, the system allows generating a shareable "
"link that anyone can use to request task access. The task creator can "
"approve or reject the request."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:182
msgid "Ergonomic Logic and Dimensions"
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:183
msgid "ERGO evaluates performance through three main pillars (ABC):"
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:185
msgid "External physical factors (Temperature, Noise, Lighting)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:186
msgid "Mental load and psychological processes (Focus, Stress, Fatigue)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:187
msgid "Action patterns during execution (Posture, Breaks, Rhythm)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:189
msgid "Personalization (Aspects)"
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:190
msgid ""
"Each user can define their own Aspects within these dimensions, allowing the "
"system to be adapted to different contexts (office, home office, factory "
"floor)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:192
msgid "Measurement units: Celsius, Decibels, Lumens, Scales (1-5), Time, etc."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:193
msgid ""
"Parametrization: Define a target value or scale for each monitored aspect."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:198
msgid "Evaluation and Differentiation"
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:199
msgid ""
"ERGO differentiates between internal perception (executor) and external "
"perception (supervisor)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:201
msgid ""
"Performed by the Executor upon completion. Represents internal perception of "
"conditions and personal efficacy."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:202
msgid ""
"Performed by the Stakeholder. Represents external perception and "
"satisfaction with the delivery."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:204
msgid ""
"Each evaluation is stored independently, allowing multiple ratings per task "
"for different executors and by different stakeholders."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:206
msgid ""
"In addition to task-level evaluation, the system maintains continuous "
"monitoring through <strong>Daily Effectiveness</strong> — a daily record "
"(scale 1-5) of the user's general productivity state. At the moment of "
"recording, the system captures a snapshot of all personalized aspects, "
"enabling correlations between ergonomic variables and performance."
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:210
msgid "Data Export for Research"
msgstr ""

#: templates/tasks/documentation.html:211
msgid ""
"ERGO offers specific CSV exports for statistical analysis in software like "
"Jamovi, SPSS and R:"
